From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] builder: backport V8's maglev Float64Min/Max fix for GCC

With the sandbox guard in place, the riscv64 build compiled every
object (2170/2176) and then failed linking mksnapshot:

  maglev-ir-riscv.cc: in function
  'v8::internal::maglev::Float64Min::GenerateCode(...)':
  undefined reference to 'void v8::internal::MacroAssembler::
  FloatMinMaxHelper<double>(FPURegister, FPURegister, FPURegister,
  MaxMinKind)'

(and the same from Float64Max::GenerateCode). FloatMinMaxHelper is a
member template declared in src/codegen/riscv/macro-assembler-riscv.h
but defined only in macro-assembler-riscv.cc, which never explicitly
instantiates it. Its only in-file users are the Float32/Float64
Min/Max wrappers. GCC inlines all four and emits no out-of-line
instantiation, so the two calls from src/maglev/riscv/maglev-ir-riscv.cc
have nothing to link against. No other object had an undefined
reference, so this is the only one.

V8's main branch has since changed maglev to call the public
MacroAssembler::Float64Min/Float64Max wrappers, which generate the same
code (each calls FloatMinMaxHelper<double> with kMin/kMax) and are
ordinary out-of-line members. Backport that change into the riscv64
GCC compat patch. The 14.4 through 15.4 lkgr branches still have the
template call.

https://github.com/riseproject-dev/python-wheels/actions/runs/35995947527/job/107620840172

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted to bpcreech/PyMiniRacer; the V8 hunk backports V8 main's switch to Float64Min/Float64Max]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 builder/0001-riscv64-gcc-compat.patch | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 builder/v8_build.py                   | 12 ++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/builder/0001-riscv64-gcc-compat.patch b/builder/0001-riscv64-gcc-compat.patch
index ee00c0f..b9b9ee3 100644
--- a/builder/0001-riscv64-gcc-compat.patch
+++ b/builder/0001-riscv64-gcc-compat.patch
@@ -34,3 +34,23 @@
      defined(HWY_NO_LIBCXX)
  #define HWY_BROKEN_EMU128 1
  #else
+--- src/maglev/riscv/maglev-ir-riscv.cc	2026-09-27 00:00:00
++++ src/maglev/riscv/maglev-ir-riscv.cc	2026-09-27 00:00:00
+@@ -881,7 +881,7 @@
+   DoubleRegister right = ToDoubleRegister(RightInput());
+   DoubleRegister out = ToDoubleRegister(result());
+ 
+-  __ FloatMinMaxHelper<double>(out, left, right, MaxMinKind::kMin);
++  __ Float64Min(out, left, right);
+ }
+ 
+ void Float64Max::SetValueLocationConstraints() {
+@@ -896,7 +896,7 @@
+   DoubleRegister right = ToDoubleRegister(RightInput());
+   DoubleRegister out = ToDoubleRegister(result());
+ 
+-  __ FloatMinMaxHelper<double>(out, left, right, MaxMinKind::kMax);
++  __ Float64Max(out, left, right);
+ }
+ 
+ int Float64Ieee754Unary::MaxCallStackArgs() const { return 0; }
diff --git a/builder/v8_build.py b/builder/v8_build.py
index b7a5c0d..498516c 100644
--- a/builder/v8_build.py
+++ b/builder/v8_build.py
@@ -408,8 +408,8 @@ def build_v8(args: Args) -> None:
         return
 
     if machine().lower() == "riscv64":
-        # Two things GCC (used instead of clang on riscv64, see is_clang=false
-        # above) genuinely cannot compile, as opposed to merely warns about
+        # Three things GCC (used instead of clang on riscv64, see is_clang=false
+        # above) genuinely cannot build, as opposed to merely warns about
         # (those are handled by treat_warnings_as_errors=false):
         #
         # * unibrow::Utf8::WriteLeadingAscii's explicit specializations are
@@ -423,6 +423,14 @@ def build_v8(args: Args) -> None:
         #   src/json/json-stringifier.cc's AppendStringSIMD asks it for a
         #   hw::FixedTag<SrcChar, 16>, which the scalar target cannot provide
         #   ("static assertion failed: Too many lanes").
+        #
+        # * src/maglev/riscv/maglev-ir-riscv.cc calls
+        #   MacroAssembler::FloatMinMaxHelper<double>, a member template
+        #   defined only in macro-assembler-riscv.cc and never explicitly
+        #   instantiated there. GCC inlines every use in that file and emits
+        #   no out-of-line copy, so linking mksnapshot fails with an undefined
+        #   reference. Call the Float64Min/Float64Max wrappers instead, as
+        #   V8's main branch now does.
         apply_patch("0001-riscv64-gcc-compat.patch")
 
     build_dir = get_v8_path() / "out.gn" / "build"
